<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gower Wassail (sung by Phil Tanner)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1949</span><span class="sg-chain-h">minor-key variant</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Here We Come A-Christmasing</span><span class="sg-chain-h">variant with &quot;Christmas&quot; in place of &quot;wassail&quot;</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Here We Come A-caroling</span><span class="sg-chain-h">variant, often sung by Americans</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">We've Been a While-A-Wandering (Yorkshire Wassail Song)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">variant</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Claymation Christmas Celebration</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1987</span><span class="sg-chain-h">satirical variants</span></li></ul></section>
